\[r = 4 \cdot \frac{\sin \theta}{\cos \theta} \cdot \frac{1}{\cos \theta}.\]Then $r \cos^2 \theta = 4 \sin \theta,$ so
\[r^2 \cos^2 \theta = 4r \sin \theta.\]Hence, $x^2 = 4y.$  This is the equation of a parabola, so the answer is $\boxed{\text{(C)}}.$

